WEBVTT

00:02:29.341 --> 00:02:31.397
and become one of their top executives.

00:02:31.798 --> 00:02:35.015
It was a job for someone
with both technical and creative skills.

00:02:35.039 --> 00:02:37.740
DF: I was trained as an architect.

00:02:37.764 --> 00:02:40.587
AG: Were you aspiring
to be someone like Frank Lloyd Wright,

00:02:40.611 --> 00:02:42.649
or did you have
a different vision in mind?

00:02:42.673 --> 00:02:45.148
DF: Sadly I really, probably didn't know

00:02:45.172 --> 00:02:46.662
who many of those people were.

00:02:47.382 --> 00:02:49.767
I was really determined
to be a comic book artist.

00:02:49.791 --> 00:02:52.072
So you could have asked me
any comic book artist,

00:02:52.096 --> 00:02:53.638
and I would have known them all.

00:02:53.662 --> 00:02:55.923
I was a kid that drew
the cover to the yearbooks

00:02:55.947 --> 00:02:57.701
and high school T-shirts and things

00:02:57.725 --> 00:02:59.066
and wanted to be an artist,

00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:01.122
and my dad told me that wasn't a real job,